-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of a flat regular local algebra with retraction
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring and let $\varpi \in R$ be an element with $\mathfrak{m}_R = (\varpi)$, i.e. the maximal ideal of $R$ is the principal ideal generated by $\varpi$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring which is a regular local ring (in Mathlib's sense, `IsRegularLocalRing`), equipped with an $R$-algebra structure such that the structure map $R \to S$ is a local homomorphism, such that $S$ is essentially of finite type over $R$ (`Algebra.EssFiniteType`), and such that $S$ is flat as an $R$-module. Assume further that there exists an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\rho \colon S \to R$, that is, a retraction of the structure map. Then the $R$-algebra $S$ is formally smooth, `Algebra.FormallySmooth R S`. Both rings are taken in the same universe. No separation or completeness hypothesis is imposed on $R$, and no hypothesis beyond the principality of $\mathfrak{m}_R$ (so $R$ is a field or a one-dimensional regular local ring, possibly non-reduced cases being excluded by noetherianity and principality only insofar as the argument uses them).
--
--   This is a ring-theoretic form of the criterion of Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud for smoothness at a rational point of a flat scheme with regular local ring over a base with principal maximal ideal. It is used in the present development to prove [`AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeHomOver.apply_closedPoint_mem_smoothLocus_of_isRegularLocalRing_stalk`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeHomOver.apply_closedPoint_mem_smoothLocus_of_isRegularLocalRing_stalk), i.e. that a section through a point whose local ring is regular lands in the smooth locus.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_algHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open IsLocalRing

theorem Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_isRegularLocalRing_of_algHom_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (ϖ : R) (hϖ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {ϖ})
    (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [IsRegularLocalRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType R S] [Module.Flat R S]
    (ρ : S →ₐ[R] R) :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth R S := by sorry
